## 2. 🎯 TARGET USER ANALYSIS

### Your Assumed Target: "General Use"

This is wrong. "General use" is not a target audience — it's an admission that you haven't identified one. Nobody wakes up thinking "I want to set up a Python server to search my photos."

### The REAL Target Audience

1. **College/University Evaluators** — the actual consumers of this project. They will review it once and never touch it again.
2. **ML hobbyists/tinkerers** — people who enjoy setting up local AI tools for fun. Tiny niche.
3. **Small-scale content creators** — photographers with 10k+ local images who are technical enough to run Python. Maybe 200 people globally.

### Who Will NEVER Use This

- Anyone without Python installed
- Anyone who uses cloud photo storage (i.e., 95% of humans)
- Anyone who values their time over tinkering with local servers
- Non-technical users (the entire "general" population)
- Mobile users (no mobile support at all)
- Anyone with more than ~50k images (it will choke — more on this below)

