## 4. 🎨 UX/UI CRITIQUE

### What feels confusing immediately

- **Monospace font everywhere** (Geist Mono as `font-sans`). The entire app uses a coding font for body text. This screams "developer project" not "product." Reading long filenames in monospace is painful.
- **The primary color is gray** (`#737373`). The primary action buttons (Search, Index) are literally gray. There is zero visual hierarchy. Nothing feels clickable or actionable.
- **Mode switching is hidden** behind a hamburger menu that defaults to collapsed. New users won't discover Image Search or Video Search modes without accidentally clicking the hamburger.
- Three separate "theme" options in settings (Mono, Light, Dark) but only one actually works — the dark/light toggle in the top-right. The theme selector in settings does nothing.

### What violates modern UX standards

| Issue | Violation |
|---|---|
| No loading skeleton / shimmer | Users see a blank void while images load |
| No error boundary | A single React crash kills the whole app |
| No undo for destructive actions | "Clear Index Data" is behind a native `window.confirm()` — not a custom modal |
| Feedback buttons have no visual state | After clicking "relevant", the button doesn't change. Was it even recorded? |
| No empty search suggestions | When the search bar is empty, show example queries. "Try: sunset, red car, person laughing" |
| Drag-and-drop is fake | The browser can't read local folder paths — you pop a modal asking the user to *type the path manually*. This defeats the purpose of drag-and-drop entirely |
| No image metadata shown | No resolution, file size, date, or path visible in results |

### What Notion/Spotify/Apple would do differently

- **Notion:** Command palette (`Ctrl+K`), instant search-as-you-type, inline previews, keyboard-first navigation
- **Spotify:** Smooth transitions between views, persistent playback bar equivalent (persistent search context), discovery-style layout
- **Apple Photos:** Grid with dynamic sizing, pinch-to-zoom grid density, timeline-based browsing, zero-config AI

