## 6. 🧪 EDGE CASE & FAILURE TESTING

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| **Empty directory** | ✅ Handles gracefully — "No valid images found" |
| **Directory with 0 images but 1000 .txt files** | ✅ Correctly filtered — returns 0,0 |
| **Corrupt image file (truncated JPEG)** | ✅ Caught in `_load_image_safely` — logged and skipped |
| **Query with special characters (`<script>alert(1)</script>`)** | ⚠️ CLIP tokenizes it harmlessly, but the query is rendered without sanitization in the frontend (`{query}` in JSX is safe by default in React) |
| **Query exactly 77 tokens** | ✅ Accepted |
| **Query > 77 tokens** | ⚠️ Silently truncated at character level (`max_chars = 77 * 4 = 308`). No user notification. |
| **10,000+ images** | 🔴 **Memory pressure.** ~20MB for embeddings + full FAISS index in RAM. Indexing takes 15-30 minutes on CPU with no progress estimate. |
| **50,000+ images** | 🔴 **Likely OOM.** 100MB+ embeddings, brute-force search becomes noticeably slow (>500ms). |
| **1-hour video at 1fps** | 🔴 **3,600 PIL images held in memory.** At ~500KB per frame, that's ~1.8GB RAM for frames alone, plus 7MB for embeddings. |
| **Network disconnect mid-search** | ⚠️ Frontend shows generic "Cannot reach server" error. No retry. No offline mode. |
| **Backend killed during indexing** | 🔴 **Data corruption risk.** `np.save()` is not atomic. A crash mid-write leaves a corrupt `.npy` file that will crash future loads. |
| **Two users indexing simultaneously** | 🔴 **Race condition.** Global `AppState` with no locking. Concurrent `index_directory` calls will corrupt the shared embeddings array. |
| **CLIP model download fails (no internet)** | ✅ Error message is clear: "Check your internet connection" |
| **Unsupported image format (.svg, .raw)** | ✅ Filtered by extension whitelist |

